  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading the drawing",
      "items": [
        "An arrow is a call: caller → callee. Only the main calls are drawn. Heavy arrows: a secured PDU going down on board A (sender build, handshake initiator). The ...RxIndication arrows of the left column: the same PDU going up on board B (receiver build, responder). The handshake messages use the SoAd and TcpIp arrows in both directions on both boards. The two builds come from one tree, one executable per board.",
        "Colours give the layer of the module's AUTOSAR namesake. This is a placement by name only.",
        "new: a directory or file that holds post-quantum code only. extended: a file of the module carries post-quantum identifiers; App_Tx.c is one of them (PqcHs_Initiate). main.c and GUIInterface.c carry such identifiers too and are not drawn.",
        "One peer: SoAd is configured with one socket connection and refuses a further one while a stream is active, and PqcHs has one instance. Every stream therefore has one receiver."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Order of the calls",
      "items": [
        "Transmit, board A: App_Tx_Submit → SecOC_TpTransmit; SecOC_MainFunctionTx authenticates and calls PduR_SecOCTransmit → SoAd_TpTransmit; SoAd_MainFunctionTx writes the PDU header and calls TcpIp_TcpTransmit → send().",
        "Receive, board B: SoAd_MainFunctionRx polls TcpIp_MainFunction: recv() → TcpIp_RxIndication → SoAd_RxIndication, which only appends the bytes to the stream buffer. SoAd_RxStreamProcess then cuts the stream into PDUs by the PDU header and calls PduR_SoAdStartOfReception, PduR_SoAdTpCopyRxData and PduR_SoAdTpRxIndication, which forward to SecOC_StartOfReception, SecOC_CopyRxData and SecOC_TpRxIndication. SecOC_MainFunctionRx checks the freshness value (FVM_GetRxFreshness fails while FVM_NoSession → PqcHs_IsEstablished reports no session), then verifies, then calls PduR_SecOCIfRxIndication → Com_RxIndication → App_Rx_RxNotification.",
        "SecOC also reports the result of each verification attempt straight to the application (the Ethernet rows use propagation mode SECOC_BOTH): SecOC_VerificationStatusCallout is defined in App_Rx.c. This call is not drawn.",
        "Transmit confirmation, not drawn: PduR_SoAdTpTxConfirmation → SecOC_TpTxConfirmation → PduR_SecOCTpTxConfirmation → Com_TpTxConfirmation → App_Tx_TxConfirmation. On the normal path the confirmation and the delivery are the two places where Com appears; App_Tx does not call Com. One more call site exists: after a confirmation with a result other than E_OK, Com_MainFunctionTx calls Com_TriggerIPDUSend → PduR_ComTransmit → SecOC_IfTransmit with Com's own Tx buffer, which the application never writes.",
        "SoAd reaches PduR and PqcHs through a table of function pointers (SoAd_UpperLayers); the route of a PDU header ID names the upper layer. The handshake messages arrive through PqcHs_SoAdTpStartOfReception, PqcHs_SoAdTpCopyRxData and PqcHs_SoAdTpRxIndication, and leave through SoAd_TpTransmit and PqcHs_SoAdTpCopyTxData."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Crypto stack",
      "items": [
        "The Csm job that a SecOC PDU row references decides between signature and MAC and supplies the key and the context string.",
        "ML-DSA-65 signs with the long-term identity key held in the Csm; the session contributes only the context string. HMAC-SHA-256 uses the session MAC keys, which PqcHs installs through Csm_KeyElementSet → CryIf_KeyElementSet → Crypto_Mac_KeyElementSet.",
        "PqcHs calls the Csm for every post-quantum operation: Csm_CustomService (ML-KEM-768 key generation, encapsulation and decapsulation, the handshake HKDF, discard of the pending secrets), Csm_SignatureGenerate and Csm_SignatureVerify (ML-DSA-65 with the handshake context), Csm_MacGenerate and Csm_MacVerify (key confirmation), Csm_KeyElementGet (key identifiers), Csm_KeyElementSet and Csm_KeySetValid (key installation).",
